## contact-forces

contact-forces-ask = Which forces act without touching?
contact-forces-title = Contact and non-contact forces
contact-forces-question = Bodies act on each other — but do they always have to touch? Five observations: a magnet and a paper clip on a thread across 2 cm of air, the same through a card, a rubbed comb over bits of paper, a block hung above the table (does friction act?), and a weight let go above the table. Which forces act without touching?
contact-forces-choices = Magnetic, electric and gravity; friction and elasticity — only when touching
contact-forces-choices-2 = None: forces pass only by touching (through the air at least)
contact-forces-choices-3 = Only the magnetic one
contact-forces-setup = A stand, a paper clip on a thread, a magnet, a card, a plastic comb, bits of paper, a block on a thread, a weight
